UID:4d069cfee1cf72e286671197c908946d@littlejumbobar.com
DESCRIPTION:A syzygy is the moment three celestial bodies fall into a sing
 le line. It is not a permanent condition. Sun\, earth\, and moon spend mos
 t of their existence scattered across the ecliptic\, and then for a few ho
 urs the geometry snaps shut and something happens: an eclipse\, a spring t
 ide\, a shadow crossing a face. Then it passes.\n\nSyzygy Trio is built on
  that principle. Three players\, three orbits\, and a music that exists on
 ly in the intervals when they line up.\n\nJay Sanders anchors the low end 
 on bass and moves to guitar and Erae Touch\, a pressure-sensitive control 
 surface that reads position\, force\, and the smallest lateral drift of a 
 fingertip. It responds less like a keyboard than like a membrane\, which m
 eans the synthesizer parts breathe and bend the way a bowed instrument doe
 s. Wil...
LOCATION:Little Jumbo: 241 Broadway St.\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://www.littlejumbobar.com/events/1976/syzygy-trio-boyd-sanders-ha
 ll
